<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- EL CONTENEDOR COMPARTIDO CON LA CARATULA.
	     El Host de .NET deja ahi la foto (Gnothi.Movil/Instantanea.cs) y los App Intents de
	     Swift la leen. Es la unica via: los App Intents solo existen en Swift y el Host esta
	     en .NET, y cruzarlos directo costaria NativeAOT y perder la carga dinamica de modulos.

	     ESTO SOLO ANDA ENTRE APPS DEL MISMO TEAM ID, que es por lo que sirve entre las dos
	     nuestras y NO serviria para que una institucion entregue la suya.

	     NO ALCANZA CON ESTE ARCHIVO: el App Group tiene que estar habilitado en el portal de
	     Apple para los dos app IDs (este y el del spike de Siri) y venir en el perfil de
	     aprovisionamiento. Si falta, GetContainerUrl devuelve null EN SILENCIO. Por eso el
	     ViewController lo escribe en el log al arrancar. -->
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.com.ncubo.gnothi</string>
	</array>

	<!-- THE INSTITUTION'S LINK, which is how a module actually arrives: the institution puts a
	     button on its page, Sonia taps it, and iOS opens Gnothi with the URL.

	     IT IS THE TWIN OF ANDROID'S App Link, and it fails in a similar way. There, without
	     AutoVerify plus a verified assetlinks.json, Chrome navigates the link itself and shows
	     DNS_PROBE_FINISHED_NXDOMAIN: the button does nothing and there is no clue. Here the
	     equivalent is the AASA, and the failure mode is the same one (Safari opens the page
	     instead of the app), so it has to be verified early and explicitly (P2 of the script).

	     WHAT THIS ALONE DOES NOT COVER: go.gnothi.app has to serve
	     /.well-known/apple-app-site-association, with no extension, as application/json, over
	     https, with no redirects, carrying the appID TEAMID.com.ncubo.gnothi.host and the
	     paths /alta* and /abrir*. And iOS CACHES it: if it is served wrong the first time, the
	     app has to be reinstalled before iOS asks for it again.

	     IN DEVELOPMENT, with no domain of our own, append ?mode=developer to the applinks
	     entry below. That makes iOS fetch the AASA straight from the domain instead of through
	     Apple's CDN, and it also needs "Associated Domains Development" switched on in
	     Settings > Developer. Android has the `pm set-app-links` shortcut for this; there is no
	     command line equivalent here. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>applinks:go.gnothi.app</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
